{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring's DataSource abstraction for the configurable Sqoop metastore to support any JDBC-compliant database without custom driver implementation",
    "Leverage the existing metrics registry service for aggregate metric retrieval to avoid duplicating core metrics logic",
    "Use Spring Boot's auto-configuration and embedded server capabilities for the Boot-based ModuleRunner to eliminate dependency on xd-containers",
    "Integrate with Spring Security's existing GlassFish (GF) native authentication support for the GF source connector to avoid custom auth implementation",
    "Reuse the existing gpfdist sink's write logic as the foundation for the jdbcgpfdist batch job's gpfdist writer to minimize redundant code",
    "Use Spring's test profile mechanism to separate mock and real repository implementations in the test infrastructure for easy environment switching",
    "Add Reactor 3.x as an optional core dependency when moving the reactor module to core to maintain backward compatibility for non-Reactor users",
    "All new REST endpoints will follow the project's existing API design conventions (HAL format, consistent error responses) for uniformity"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All existing related code (gpfdist sink, metrics registry, legacy ModuleRunner, reactor module, test infrastructure) is present and functional, requiring only modification rather than ground-up development",
    "Target custom databases for Sqoop metastore are supported by Spring JDBC (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle) with no additional custom driver requirements",
    "The existing XD-2287 HDFS-backed module registry implementation is complete and only requires documentation updates, no code changes",
    "GlassFish (GF) native authentication properties are already exposed via Spring's configuration properties mechanism, requiring only minor connector updates and documentation",
    "The existing metrics registry provides programmatic access to all counters, gauges, and rich-gauges, requiring only the addition of aggregate REST endpoints",
    "The current test infrastructure's mock/real repository coupling is limited to configuration and classpath dependencies, with no deep architectural coupling requiring major rework",
    "Reactor 3.x is compatible with Spring Framework 6.0's reactive programming model, with no conflicting dependency versions",
    "All user stories are independent, with no cross-cutting dependencies requiring coordinated changes across multiple features"
  ],
